4. Convert this traditional class to a Java Record with compact constructor validation:
public final class Coordinate {
    private final double latitude;
    private final double longitude;
    public Coordinate(double latitude, double longitude) {
        if (latitude < -90 || latitude > 90) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid lat");
        if (longitude < -180 || longitude > 180) throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid long");
        this.latitude = latitude;
        this.longitude = longitude;
    }
    public double getLatitude()  { return latitude; }
    public double getLongitude() { return longitude; }
    // + equals, hashCode, toString omitted for brevity
